## Arize connects human review verdicts to agent prompt tests

Source: Arize AI — https://arize.com/blog/how-to-build-a-software-factory-that-tests-its-own-prompts/
Published: 2026-10-22
Channel: news

Arize AX records how AI agents run and helps teams test changes to them. In a new walkthrough, Jim Bennett connects decisions from a coding pipeline to the exact agent runs and prompts that produced its work. Each issue has one trace, with smaller operation records called spans for individual stages. Prompt versions and pull-request identifiers keep later review outcomes connected to their origins.

The pipeline collects the human review gate’s first verdict, test outcomes and subsequent reversions. It distinguishes missed problems from false alarms rather than hiding both inside one agreement score. For example, the author describes reviewers approving code that fetched additional review data but never used it in the displayed result.

Candidate reviewer prompts are tested in read-only checkouts pinned to reviewed commits. Promotion requires fewer misses without more false alarms. The reported improvement used the same cases for development and testing; it is not evidence of better performance on unseen code. Human verdicts also need auditing.

Why it matters: Agent-review owners should preserve verdicts and test proposed prompt changes against pinned examples.

