## Weave updates token and finish-reason names in AI traces

Source: Weights & Biases — https://github.com/wandb/weave/releases/tag/v0.53.13
Published: 2026-10-22
Channel: github

Weave captures AI application activity so engineers can inspect model calls and evaluate results. Its 0.53.13 release updates the names used for several OpenTelemetry generative-AI attributes, the named fields attached to a model-call record. A field-name change can affect dashboards and stored data even when the model call itself still succeeds.

For illustration, a team tracking prompt-cache writes could see an apparently missing count if its query expects the older field name. Python and Node emitters now use gen_ai.usage.cache_write.input_tokens for cache-write tokens and gen_ai.usage.reasoning.output_tokens for reasoning output tokens. The implementation also moves finish reasons out of individual output messages; Google ADK and Pi coding-agent records emit the span-level gen_ai.response.finish_reasons field instead.

The linked change explicitly requires corresponding server support first. Only the new names are emitted, and an older server can drop the cache-write count and per-message finish reasons. This is a compatibility migration, not evidence of lower token usage or better model quality. Check the server version and representative traces before changing production emitters.

Why it matters: Telemetry owners using Weave should coordinate server and emitter upgrades, then check token queries and finish-reason fields.

